    },
    {
      "id": "Q3",
      "title": "Colour correction fit",
      "status": "done",
      "notes": "Tested M1/M2/M3 in sRGB and linear light on cluster-balanced flat samples with dark/bright anchors and Huber loss. Selected M2_srgb: held-out DE00 = 3.703 vs in-sample 3.864 (gap -0.161 <= 1.0), beating M1_srgb (5.043) and M2_linear (3.806) while generalizing better cross-pair A->B than M3_srgb (7.136 vs 7.701 DE00) with 22 vs 73 params. Recorded Joint and per-pair params, observed channel ranges, and exported 33^3 look.cube (will update after joint refit with spatial stages)."
    },
    {
      "id": "Q4",
      "title": "Gradient / lower-area darkening",
      "status": "done",
      "notes": "2D surface R^2: vertical 70.2%/75.7% vs radial vignette 6.4%/0.5%. Visual inspection of row profiles confirmed pure smoothstep multiply gradient starting at y0=0.1733 and saturating at y1=0.7281 (strength_rgb=[0.250636, 0.255053, 0.292137]). Row-mean y correlation dropped from -0.9393/-0.9309 to -0.3514 (A) and +0.2994 (B). Full flat_interior median DE00: 2.408 (A), 2.775 (B)."
